---
import { DISCORD, REPO, doc, url, type Lang } from '../i18n'

interface Props {
  lang: Lang
}
const { lang } = Astro.props

const content = {
  en: {
    eyebrow: 'Open source · GitHub Actions · Docker Compose · Tailscale',
    title: 'A private preview of every pull request, on a machine you own',
    lead: 'Open a pull request and a complete copy of your application starts on your own Linux box, with its own database copied from a long-lived baseline of your default branch. You get a private HTTPS address that only devices in your tailnet can open. Every push updates it, and closing the PR removes it.',
    ctaStart: 'Get started',
    ctaGithub: 'View on GitHub',
    flow: [
      'pull request ──▶ GitHub Actions on your machine (self-hosted runner)',
      '                   │  build images · copy the baseline’s data · run the PR’s migrations · start',
      '                   ▼',
      '   https://myapp-pr-42.<your tailnet>.ts.net      private to your tailnet',
    ],
    featuresTitle: 'Why tailnet-preview',
    features: [
      {
        title: 'Realistic upgrades',
        body: 'Each PR starts from a copy of real (demo) data and runs its own migrations, the way production will. Bugs that only show up on an existing database appear before you merge.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Private',
        body: 'No public port, tunnel or login page. Only devices in your Tailscale network can reach the environments.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Cheap',
        body: 'Any Linux box with Docker, such as a home server or a spare VM. One machine serves many projects.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Any stack',
        body: 'Bash and Docker Compose. Your database is just a service in your compose file, and your existing compose file stays as it is.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tells you what went wrong',
        body: 'A comment on the PR gives the address, or names the cause of a failed deploy and how to fix it.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Works with AI agents',
        body: 'The docs are step-by-step procedures. Paste one prompt into your coding agent and it does the setup, telling you which steps only you can do.',
      },
    ],
    agentTitle: 'Using an AI coding agent?',
    agentLead: 'Open it in your project and paste this prompt:',
    agentPrompt:
      'Set up tailnet-preview (https://github.com/riverscn/tailnet-preview) for this project, so every pull request gets its own preview environment on my machine. Follow its docs/agent-guide.md. Tell me which steps only I can do, all at once, and never ask me for a secret in the chat.',
    howTitle: 'How it works',
    howLead:
      'Each environment is a Docker Compose project with your services, database included. To copy the baseline, the engine pauses it for a few seconds and copies its data volumes.',
    howHead: ['Environment', 'Data', 'Lifetime'],
    how: [
      [
        '<code>main</code>, the baseline',
        'Created once (migrate + seed), then upgraded by every push to the default branch',
        'Long-lived',
      ],
      [
        '<code>pr-&lt;number&gt;</code>',
        'A copy of the baseline’s data volumes (database, uploads…), then the PR’s migrations',
        'Until the PR closes',
      ],
      [
        '<code>br-&lt;branch&gt;</code> (optional)',
        'The same, for a branch without a PR, when the workflow opts in',
        'Until the branch is deleted or gets a PR',
      ],
    ],
    modesTitle: 'Two ways to reach environments',
    modes: [
      {
        name: 'sidecar',
        tag: 'default',
        addr: 'https://&lt;project&gt;-&lt;env&gt;.&lt;tailnet&gt;.ts.net',
        body: 'Each environment is its own Tailscale node with its own certificate. Needs nothing beyond Tailscale. A new environment’s certificate is often only issued minutes after the deploy.',
      },
      {
        name: 'shared',
        tag: 'optional',
        addr: 'https://&lt;project&gt;-&lt;env&gt;.&lt;your domain&gt;',
        body: 'One entry point per machine with one wildcard certificate, so previews work right away. Needs a domain whose DNS provider has an API, and a split DNS entry in the tailnet.',
      },
    ],
    dayTitle: 'Day to day',
    dayLead:
      'Everything runs from GitHub Actions. On the machine, the same engine helps when something looks wrong.',
    needTitle: 'What you need',
    need: [
      'A Linux machine with Docker that stays on, with a few GB of free memory.',
      'A Tailscale account. The free plan works.',
      'A GitHub repository you control, private or with the precautions in the security guide.',
      'An application that runs in containers and reads its URL and database connection from environment variables.',
    ],
    statusTitle: 'Status',
    status:
      'Pre-1.0 (0.x), in daily use by the multi-tenant SaaS project it was extracted from. Linux hosts only. Pull requests from forks are never deployed.',
    community: 'Questions or help with a setup',
    communityLink: 'Join the Discord server',
  },
  'zh-cn': {
    eyebrow: '开源 · GitHub Actions · Docker Compose · Tailscale',
    title: '每个 PR 一套私有试用环境，跑在你自己的机器上',
    lead: '开一个 PR，你自己的 Linux 机器上就会起一套完整的应用，数据库从默认分支的常驻基线复制而来。你会得到一个私有的 HTTPS 地址，只有你 tailnet 里的设备能打开。往 PR 推送会更新它，关闭 PR 它就删除。',
    ctaStart: '快速开始',
    ctaGithub: '在 GitHub 上查看',
    flow: [
      'pull request ──▶ GitHub Actions（你机器上的 self-hosted runner）',
      '                   │  构建镜像 · 复制基线数据 · 执行 PR 的迁移 · 启动',
      '                   ▼',
      '   https://myapp-pr-42.<你的 tailnet>.ts.net      只在 tailnet 内可访问',
    ],
    featuresTitle: '为什么用 tailnet-preview',
    features: [
      {
        title: '贴近真实的升级',
        body: '每个 PR 都从一份真实（演示）数据的副本开始，再执行它自己的迁移，和上线时一样。只在已有数据上才会出现的问题，合并前就能发现。',
      },
      { title: '私有', body: '没有公网端口、隧道或登录页：只有你 Tailscale 网络里的设备能访问这些环境。' },
      { title: '便宜', body: '任何装了 Docker 的 Linux 机器都行，比如家里的小主机或一台闲置虚拟机。一台机器可以服务多个项目。' },
      { title: '不挑技术栈', body: '只用 Bash 和 Docker Compose。数据库就是 compose 文件里的一个服务，项目原有的 compose 文件不用改。' },
      { title: '出错时告诉你原因', body: 'PR 上的评论给出地址；部署失败时，会写明原因和处理办法。' },
      {
        title: '适合 AI 编程助手',
        body: '文档都是一步步的操作手册。把一段提示词粘贴给编程助手，它就能完成接入，并告诉你哪些步骤只能由你亲自完成。',
      },
    ],
    agentTitle: '在用 AI 编程助手？',
    agentLead: '在你的项目里打开它，粘贴这段提示词：',
    agentPrompt:
      '为这个项目接入 tailnet-preview（https://github.com/riverscn/tailnet-preview），让每个 PR 都在我的主机上有自己的试用环境。按它的 docs/agent-guide.zh-CN.md 来做。需要我亲自做的步骤一次性告诉我，永远不要在聊天里向我索要密钥。',
    howTitle: '原理',
    howLead: '每个环境是一个 Docker Compose 项目，包含你的所有服务，数据库也在内。复制基线时，引擎让基线暂停几秒，复制它的数据卷。',
    howHead: ['环境', '数据', '生命周期'],
    how: [
      ['<code>main</code>，即基线', '第一次创建时执行迁移并灌演示数据，之后每次推送默认分支时原地升级', '常驻'],
      ['<code>pr-&lt;编号&gt;</code>', '复制基线的数据卷（数据库、上传文件等），再执行 PR 的迁移', '到 PR 关闭为止'],
      ['<code>br-&lt;分支&gt;</code>（可选）', '同上，用于没有 PR 的分支，需要在工作流里开启', '到分支删除或开了 PR 为止'],
    ],
    modesTitle: '两种访问方式',
    modes: [
      {
        name: 'sidecar',
        tag: '默认',
        addr: 'https://&lt;项目&gt;-&lt;环境&gt;.&lt;tailnet&gt;.ts.net',
        body: '每个环境是一个独立的 Tailscale 节点，有自己的证书。除了 Tailscale 不需要别的。新环境的证书常常要在部署几分钟后才签发。',
      },
      {
        name: 'shared',
        tag: '可选',
        addr: 'https://&lt;项目&gt;-&lt;环境&gt;.&lt;你的域名&gt;',
        body: '每台机器一个入口、一张通配符证书，环境部署完立刻能打开。需要一个 DNS 服务商提供 API 的域名，并在 tailnet 里配置 split DNS。',
      },
    ],
    dayTitle: '日常使用',
    dayLead: '一切都由 GitHub Actions 驱动。在机器上，同一个引擎可以帮你排查问题。',
    needTitle: '需要准备什么',
    need: [
      '一台装了 Docker、一直开着的 Linux 机器，留出几 GB 空闲内存。',
      '一个 Tailscale 账号，免费套餐就够用。',
      '一个你能管理的 GitHub 仓库，最好是私有的；公开仓库要按安全说明采取措施。',
      '一个能在容器里运行、从环境变量读取自己地址和数据库连接的应用。',
    ],
    statusTitle: '状态',
    status:
      '1.0 之前（0.x），已在它所源自的多租户 SaaS 项目中日常使用。只支持 Linux 主机。来自 fork 的 PR 永远不会被部署。',
    community: '有问题或需要帮忙接入',
    communityLink: '加入 Discord 服务器',
  },
}[lang]

const cli = `$ tailnet-preview list
main       3f6fd43dd417  https://myapp-main.tail1234.ts.net
pr-42      d69d97d1ab55  https://myapp-pr-42.tail1234.ts.net
$ tailnet-preview doctor pr-42      # containers, Tailscale, HTTPS, upstreams, logs
$ tailnet-preview reset pr-42       # copy the baseline again`
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">{content.eyebrow}</p>
    <h1>{content.title}</h1>
    <p class="lead">{content.lead}</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={url(lang, '/getting-started/')}>{content.ctaStart} →</a>
      <a class="button" href={REPO}>{content.ctaGithub}</a>
    </div>
    <pre class="flow" aria-label="pull request → self-hosted runner → private URL">{content.flow.join('\n')}</pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <h2>{content.featuresTitle}</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {
      content.features.map((f) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h3>{f.title}</h3>
          <p>{f.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <div class="agent">
    <h2>{content.agentTitle}</h2>
    <p>{content.agentLead}</p>
    <pre class="prompt">{content.agentPrompt}</pre>
    <p class="small">
      <a href={doc(lang, 'docs/agent-guide')}>{lang === 'en' ? 'Read the agent guide' : '阅读 AI 助手指南'} →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <h2>{content.howTitle}</h2>
  <p class="muted">{content.howLead}</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>{content.howHead.map((h) => <th>{h}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          content.how.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              {row.map((cell) => (
                <td set:html={cell} />
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small"><a href={doc(lang, 'docs/design')}>docs/design →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <h2>{content.modesTitle}</h2>
  <div class="grid two">
    {
      content.modes.map((m) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h3>
            <code>{m.name}</code> <span class="tag">{m.tag}</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="addr" set:html={m.addr} />
          <p>{m.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section split">
  <div>
    <h2>{content.dayTitle}</h2>
    <p class="muted">{content.dayLead}</p>
    <pre>{cli}</pre>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h2>{content.needTitle}</h2>
    <ul class="checks">{content.need.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}</ul>
    <h3>{content.statusTitle}</h3>
    <p class="muted">{content.status}</p>
    <p>
      {content.community}: <a href={DISCORD}>{content.communityLink}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <div class="cta">
    <h2>{lang === 'en' ? 'Ready to try it?' : '准备好试试了吗？'}</h2>
    <a class="button primary" href={url(lang, '/getting-started/')}>{content.ctaStart} →</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero {
    background:
      radial-gradient(1200px 400px at 50% -100px, var(--accent-soft), transparent 70%),
      var(--bg);
    padding: 72px 0 40px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .hero-inner {
    max-width: 880px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 auto 28px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .flow {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .section {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr));
  }
  .grid.two {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
  }
  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 20px 22px;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }
  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .card p + p {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .card .addr {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .agent {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 28px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent-soft), var(--bg-soft));
  }
  .prompt {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .split {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .checks {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .checks li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 40px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
